  <section class="cv-section">
    <h3>Research Appointments</h3>
    <div class="cv-entry">
      <div class="cv-entry-top">
        <span><strong>Research Assistant</strong>, Sustainability, Optimization, Learning, and Algorithms Research Lab (SOLAR), UMass Amherst</span>
        <span class="cv-dates">2022–current</span>
      </div>
      <p class="cv-note">
        Large-scale data science and algorithm research for sustainability and equity. Publication collaborations with CMU, MIT, and Columbia.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Wrote the <a href="https://github.com/coopersigrist/SunSight" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SunSight</a> library for policy simulation and
          visualization of national-scale, ZIP-code granularity solar deployment and its effects on energy generation, carbon emissions, and equity.
        </li>
        <li>
          Cleaned and analyzed large-scale data from
          <a href="https://sunroof.withgoogle.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's Project Sunroof</a>, the American Community Survey, EIA,
          and others.
        </li>
        <li>Developed a multi-objective optimizing evolutionary neural network method for rooftop solar panel placement.</li>
        <li>
          Simulated effects of incentives and tariffs on consumer behavior and solar deployment; drafting alternative policies from statistics,
          simulation, and machine learning.
        </li>
        <li>Created, formalized, and analyzed the Green Bin Packing problem for carbon-efficient job allocation in data centers.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="cv-entry">
      <div class="cv-entry-top">
        <span><strong>Research Assistant</strong>, Biologically Inspired Neuro-Dynamical Systems Lab (BINDS), UMass Amherst</span>
        <span class="cv-dates">2018–2022</span>
      </div>
      <p class="cv-note">Low-energy, biologically plausible machine learning models and theoretical analysis.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Major contributor of the <a href="https://github.com/BindsNET/bindsnet" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BindsNET</a> library for spiking
          neural network simulation.
        </li>
        <li>Developed a minibatching procedure for spiking-neuron training on large-scale networks.</li>
        <li>Theoretically analyzed the computational power of a spiking neuron compared to artificial neurons.</li>
        <li>Developed a circuit simulation method using graph neural networks with 100% accuracy.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
